BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Understanding Latin America’s Economy in the Twenty-first Centur
 y
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T213000
DTSTAMP:20261028T061106Z
UID:c3d78f5dcaf5a9aa@gid-seminars.wnprc.wisc.edu
CATEGORIES:Lecture/Presentation/Talk
DESCRIPTION:Latin America’s economic performance is often depicted as a 
 long sequence of repeated failures\, including its contribution to global 
 financial crises as well as its slow growth and intractable inequalities. 
 Its experience in the twenty-first century\, however\, reveals considerabl
 e and underappreciated successes (as well as setbacks). This talk will rev
 iew the region's growth and development in the last quarter century\, incl
 uding the commodity boom\, a surprising decline in economic inequality\, r
 esponses to the financial and Covid-19 crises\, and the emergence of left-
 leaning governments that opted for pragmatic and orthodox macro policies m
 ixed with innovative antipoverty programs.\n\nLivestream Link\n\nJeff Dayt
 on-Johnson has served as vice president of academic affairs and dean at th
 e Middlebury Institute of International Studies at Monterey since 2014. He
  is also a professor of international policy & development there. Prior to
  joining MIIS\, he was senior economist for Latin America & the Caribbean 
 at the OECD Development Centre in Paris\, and assistant and associate prof
 essor of economics and international development studies at Dalhousie Univ
 ersity in Canada. Dayton-Johnson's research and teaching interests include
  economic development\, inequality\, Latin America & the Caribbean\, publi
 c policy\, migration\, social cohesion. He earned a PhD in economics and a
 n AB hons in Latin American Studies at UC Berkeley.\n\nEvent URL: https://
 events.stanford.edu/event/understanding-latin-americas-economy-in-the-twen
 ty-first-century\n\nSource: stanford_virtual
LOCATION:Bolivar House
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/understanding-latin-americas-economy
 -in-the-twenty-first-century
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Reminder: Understanding Latin America’s Economy in the Twent
 y-first Century
TRIGGER:-PT1H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
