BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Zeming Lin and Roshan Rao from Biohub - Day 1
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261029T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261029T160000
DTSTAMP:20261028T061106Z
UID:22e82769191c4a51@gid-seminars.wnprc.wisc.edu
CATEGORIES:Talks
DESCRIPTION:More info for both days and livestream links at broad.io/biohu
 b-broad-2026. \n\n \n\nThursday\, October 29\n\nTitle: World models of pro
 tein biology\nLocation: Broad Auditorium (415M-1-Auditorium)\nTime: 11:00 
 am - 12:00 pm\nSpeaker: Zeming Lin\, Biohub\n\n\nAbstract: Protein languag
 e models learn representations of sequence and structure that support the 
 prediction of biomolecular complexes and the design of proteins with exper
 imentally measured binding activity. Biohub's open release of the ESM fami
 ly of world models – ESMC\, ESMFold2\, and ESM Atlas – makes these cap
 abilities available to the broader research community. Using ESMC and ESMF
 old2 to search candidate sequences\, the team designed minibinders and sin
 gle-chain antibodies against five targets. Additional inference-time searc
 h improved experimental hit rates in nine of ten target-modality compariso
 ns. The ESMAtlas gives a perspective on scientific discovery with interpre
 table ESM features.\n\nThese advances make structure prediction and large-
 scale computational search increasingly accessible\, while experimental va
 lidation remains a central constraint on biological discovery. Model confi
 dence can help prioritize candidates\, but establishing binding\, specific
 ity\, and function requires experimental evidence. The cost and timescale 
 of obtaining that evidence limit how rapidly computational hypotheses can 
 be evaluated and refined. In this talk\, Zeming Lin will examine how resea
 rchers can use these models for prediction and design\, and how virtual bi
 ology might accelerate experimental throughput.\n\nBiography: Zeming Lin i
 s a Principal Research Scientist in AI Research at Biohub and a co-founder
  of EvolutionaryScale. His research focuses on large-scale protein models 
 for structure prediction and protein design. He was the main modeling cont
 ributor to ESMFold\, which predicts atomic-level protein structures direct
 ly from sequence\, and helped develop ESM3 and Biohub's recent ESMFold2. E
 arlier\, at Meta FAIR\, he was a member of the in\n\nEvent URL: https://ev
 ents.broadinstitute.org/event/zeming-lin-and-roshan-rao-from-biohub-day-1
 \n\nSource: broad_institute
LOCATION:Merkin Building (415M)\, Broad Auditorium
URL:https://events.broadinstitute.org/event/zeming-lin-and-roshan-rao-from
 -biohub-day-1
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Reminder: Zeming Lin and Roshan Rao from Biohub - Day 1
TRIGGER:-PT1H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
