BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ENT Experts Up Close: Updates in Parotid Masses and Sinonasal Mali
 gnancies
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T210000
DTSTAMP:20261028T061106Z
UID:47be8dd19a2912a3@gid-seminars.wnprc.wisc.edu
CATEGORIES:Class/Seminar
DESCRIPTION:OverviewThis one-hour CME activity offers a concise\, evidence
 -based update on the evaluation\, diagnosis\, and management of parotid ma
 sses and sinonasal malignancies. Topics cover contemporary imaging\, patho
 logy interpretation\, surgical approaches\, as well as adjuvant and system
 ic therapies. The session emphasizes multidisciplinary decision-making\, f
 unctional outcomes (including facial nerve preservation and skull base con
 siderations)\, survivorship\, and select endoscopic and minimally invasive
  techniques. Attendees will leave with useful takeaways to support clinica
 l decision-making\, streamline referrals\, and stay current on evolving tr
 eatment options and clinical trials.\n\nRegistrationRegistration for all p
 ractitioners - free\n\nTo register for this activity\, please click HERE.
 \n\nCreditsAMA PRA Category 1 Credits™ (1.00 hours)\, Non-Physician Part
 icipation Credit (1.00 hours)\n\nTarget AudienceSpecialties - Allergy\, Im
 munology\, and Rheumatology\, Otolaryngology (ENT)Professions - Advance Pr
 actice Nurse (APN)\, Fellow/Resident\, Non-Physician\, Nurse\, Physician\,
  Registered Nurse (RN)\n ObjectivesAt the conclusion of this activity\, le
 arners should be able to:\n1. Describe types of molecular testing availabl
 e for parotid masses \n2. Review the contraindications and indications for
  parotidectomy\n3. Identify updates in diagnostic workup and staging crite
 ria for sinonasal malignancies\n4. Describe emerging systemic therapies an
 d active clinical trials relevant to sinonasal cancer management\n\nAccred
 itationIn support of improving patient care\, Stanford Medicine is jointly
  accredited by the Accreditation Council for Continuing Medical Education 
 (ACCME)\, the Accreditation Council for Pharmacy Education (ACPE)\, and th
 e American Nurses Credentialing Center (ANCC)\, to provide continuing educ
 ation for the healthcare team. \n \nCredit Designation \nAmerican Medical 
 Association (AMA) \nStanford Medicine designates this Live Activity for a 
 maximum of 1.00 AMA PRA Category 1 CreditsTM.  Physicians shou\n\nEvent UR
 L: https://events.stanford.edu/event/ent-experts-up-close-updates-in-parot
 id-masses-and-sinonasal-malignancies\n\nSource: stanford_virtual
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/ent-experts-up-close-updates-in-paro
 tid-masses-and-sinonasal-malignancies
