 orpuz\, MD\, MBA\nTalk Title: Long-Acting Injectable Antiretroviral Therap
 y for Viremic Patients in a Low-Barrier Clinic\nBio: Carlos Gabriel Corpuz
 \, MD\, MBA\, is an Infectious Diseases fellow at the University of Washin
 gton and an MPH student in Epidemiology. He provides HIV primary care at M
 adison Clinic and conducts research through a T32 training grant. His rese
 arch examines the implementation of long-acting injectable antiretroviral 
 therapy across HIV care settings\, with a focus on reaching patients with 
 viremia\, equitable access\, and treatment outcomes. His broader interests
  include improving how healthcare programs adopt new evidence and organize
  care to meet patients’ needs.\n\nEvent URL: https://washington.zoom.us/
 meeting/register/Jppi1gfIQlOsxJcbmoq0kA\n\nSource: uw_cfar
