SUMMARY:Stanford Emergency Medicine Innovation Symposium - StEMI X
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T220000
DTSTAMP:20261028T061106Z
UID:745c471efeda7ff2@gid-seminars.wnprc.wisc.edu
CATEGORIES:Lecture/Presentation/Talk
DESCRIPTION:AI is reshaping diagnosis. Digital health is redefining access
 . Acute care is evolving fast.\n\nThe Stanford Emergency Medicine Innovati
 on Symposium - StEMI X - brings together the clinicians\, technologists\, 
 operators\, investors\, and policymakers who are building what comes next.
  StEMI X is the first and largest virtual global conference on innovation 
 in acute care.CME will be offered for attendance. Shiv Rao\, MD\, founder 
 and CEO of Abridge will offer the keynote\, joined by 30+ expert speakers 
 from around the country.\n\nSessions include:\n\nThe Augmented ED: Levelin
 g Up Your Clinical Practice with Next-Gen AI\n\nThe AI Minefield: Navigati
 ng Ethics\, Bias\, and Safety in Clinical Care\n\nSee One\, Do One\, Teach
  One\, Prompt One: Medical Education in the AI Era\n\nCo-Pilot or Replacem
 ent? Reclaiming the Physician’s Role in the Age of AI\n\nYear in Review:
  Top 10 acute care technology research papers of 2026\n\nSignal vs. Noise:
  What's Real and What's Not in the Next Generation of Medical Hardware\n\n
 Building Safer Waiting Rooms: Using Tech to Solve the "Right Patient\, Rig
 ht Time" Puzzle\n\nTelemedicine in Acute Care: From the ED to the Home\n\n
 Design Thinking in the ED: Turning frontline insight into better solutions
 \n\nThe Innovation Ecosystem: Bridging the Gap Between Industry and the Fr
 ont Lines\n\nBedside to Boardroom: A Blueprint for Building a High-Impact 
 Acute Care Startup\n\nWinning the C-Suite: The Art of securing institution
 al buy-in for emerging technologies\n\nEvent URL: https://events.stanford.
 edu/event/stanford-emergency-medicine-innovation-symposium-stemi-x-4077\n
 \nSource: stanford_virtual
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/stanford-emergency-medicine-innovati
 on-symposium-stemi-x-4077
